    "title": "🚨 Crash on I-280 in Redwood City Injures Two, Sparks Brush Fire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "21 hours ago Two people were hurt Tuesday evening when a car hit an embankment and caught fire along southbound I‑280 , just south of Edgewood Road in Redwood City . The crash happened around 6 p.m. , according to the California Highway Patrol . Fire crews from Cal Fire San Mateo–Santa Cruz Unit contained the resulting blaze to about half an acre after flames spread through eucalyptus trees and briefly jumped the freeway. Both the driver and passenger were taken to a local hospital with minor injuries . As of 8:40 p.m. , the far right lane of southbound I‑280 remained closed. Motorists should expect possible lingering delays in the area.\nMore Info: CA Crash Injures Two, Sparks Half-Acre Fire",
